              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CLYN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy-Creamy-Quick and Easy! Made me wish I had some coconut on hand to toss into the filling! Note* Could easily have made two pies. Had a bunch left over to eat straight from the mixing bowl!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is just delicious!! Next time I will use a bigger pie shell a 10 inch, I couldn't quite get it all in the one I had. Or to get it to fit better in the 9 inch I will use a smaller can of pineapple. So creamy, gone in seconds!",
            "datePublished": "2002-05-10T16:54:16.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beth Cheeves Culpepper"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good, I added 4 oz cream cheese and this made it creamer and firmer. Very tasty.",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-01T19:43:40.487Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clc408"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So easy and delicious. The filling amount was perfect for a 10\" pie. If the filling seems too runny, make sure you press ALL the juice from the pineapple before folding in. Also, take the small extra step to whip some real cream instead of the Cool Whip. You won't be sorry. I garnished mine with some toasted coconut.",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-09T19:50:27.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pat-Perry"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this to bring in to work as a nice summertime dessert. One of my co workers requested something with pineapple. I chose this, no bake since we are currently swimming in humidity. I decided to double the recipe and make it in a 9X12. I just emptied 2 graham cracker pie crusts into a bowl, added a little melted butter and some of the pineapple juice. Layered it on the bottom and doubled everything else. Covered it all in snowy white coconut. It looked amazing. After spending the night in the fridge it made the trip to work. People said they liked it and a few took some home for later but there were left overs. It was not a total hit. Granted not everyone likes/loves pineapple or coconut. For myself, I found it almost too sweet. Cool and refreshing yes, but just too rich for me. Wondered how it would taste frozen though. Although I am glad I made this I doubt I will be making it again.",
            "datePublished": "2026-08-05T19:16:47.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tugboatwilly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had read some of the reviews before making this and heeded the advice about using a 10 inch pie shell. The one change I made was use some chopped mandarin oranges in place of about a third of the pineapple. I also topped it with coconut. Just because I really love coconut. It was delicious while being fairly light. It was gone in just a couple days. I will make it again.",
            "datePublished": "2019-08-02T13:42:15.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KaylaMayaCamrynMOM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added 4 oz of cream cheese to this and I am glad I did. I do not see how this would set up without something a little thicker in the mix. I ended up freezing it to get it thick enough to hold together. The flavor was wonderful though.",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-23T07:12:09.370Z"
